Third-party notices
===================

This package is released under Apache-2.0. It bundles no third-party data. It
reads, or can be pointed at, the resources listed below; each keeps its own terms
and its own access route, and none of them is redistributed here.

Auxiliary public resources
--------------------------

OptimusKG
  Version: Harvard Dataverse deposit doi:10.7910/DVN/IYNGEV.
  Access route: public repository and Dataverse deposit, no account required.
  Licence: MIT for the code, CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 for the data.
  Source: https://github.com/mims-harvard/OptimusKG
  Role: substrate for the knowledge-graph path retrieval agent. Only the schema,
        node kinds, relation types and release-date semantics are mirrored here.

Hetionet
  Version: v1.0. Access route: direct download. Licence: CC0 1.0.
  Source: https://github.com/hetio/hetionet
  Role: cross-validation of substrate generalisation.

Human-GEM
  Version: v2.0.1. Access route: public repository release. Licence: CC-BY 4.0.
  Source: https://github.com/SysBioChalmers/Human-GEM/releases/tag/v2.0.1
  Role: source of the metabolic reaction edges and of the context-specific flux
        model. The release ships a reduced reconstruction of the named pathways
        plus a reader for the released JSON export.

Reactome
  Access route: public download. Licence: CC0.
  Source: https://reactome.org/download-data
  Role: pathway membership edges.

KEGG
  Access route: public pathway database. Licence: academic use; no commercial
  reuse terms are granted by the provider.
  Source: https://www.genome.jp/kegg/pathway.html
  Role: colorectal cancer pathway map and pathway-to-disease context.

DepMap
  Version: DepMap Public 26Q1, released 2026-04-01.
  Access route: public portal download, no account required.
  Licence: CC-BY 4.0 under the DepMap terms.
  Source: https://depmap.org/portal/data_page/?tab=allData
  Role: CRISPR Chronos gene-effect scores and the CCLE metabolomics table.

GDSC
  Version: Release 8.4. Access route: public FTP. Licence: CC-BY 4.0 under the
  Sanger standard terms.
  Source: https://ftp.sanger.ac.uk/pub/project/cancerrxgene/releases/
  Role: drug sensitivity.

PRISM Repositioning
  Access route: DepMap portal download. Licence: CC-BY 4.0.
  Source: https://depmap.org/repurposing/
  Role: drug response.

LINCS L1000 Connectivity Map
  Version: CMap 2020 Level 5. Access route: public portal. Licence: CC0.
  Source: https://clue.io/data/CMap2020
  Role: transcriptional response signatures.

GDC
  Version: GDC Data Release 46, projects TCGA-COAD and TCGA-READ.
  Access route: open public tier; raw sequence reads under dbGaP phs000178.
  Licence: GDC open-tier terms.
  Source: https://portal.gdc.cancer.gov
  Role: colorectal adenocarcinoma expression and clinical export.

cBioPortal
  Study: coadread_tcga_pan_can_atlas_2018.
  Access route: public instance. Licence: cBioPortal public-instance terms.
  Source: https://www.cbioportal.org/study/summary?id=coadread_tcga_pan_can_atlas_2018
  Role: cross-cohort expression context.

GEO
  Series: GSE35452, GSE45404, GSE68204, GSE119409, GSE150082.
  Access route: public deposit. Licence: GEO public-deposit terms.
  Source: https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/geo/
  Role: pretreatment-biopsy expression with pathological response.

EBI MetaboLights
  Access route: public portal. Licence: EMBL-EBI terms of use.
  Source: https://www.ebi.ac.uk/metabolights/
  Role: open metabolomics route.

Human Metabolome Database
  Version: HMDB 5.0. Access route: browser only; the portal returns HTTP 403 to
  automated access as checked on 2026-09-17.
  Licence: free for academic use.
  Source: https://hmdb.ca
  Role: cited bibliographically for metabolite identity only; not accessed
        programmatically by this package.

Gated and private resources
---------------------------

The retrospective and prospective clinical arms are held at their institutions
under their own data-use agreements and are never redistributed. The in vitro
cell-line corroboration is laboratory work and is not part of this package.

